iris: never advertise the Xe2 CCS DRM modifiers

Third and final half of the same de-advertisement:

  kernel-patches/7.1/chromeos/0002-lnl_bmg_ccs_deadvertise.patch  display planes
  mesa-patches/0003-isl-do-not-advertise-xe2-ccs-modifiers.patch  ANV
  this patch                                                      iris

0003 alone was not enough, because iris does not share ANV's modifier
filtering. ANV asks isl_drm_modifier_get_score() in src/intel/isl/isl_drm.c;
iris has its own modifier_is_supported() in
src/gallium/drivers/iris/iris_resource.c, which gates the Xe2 CCS modifiers
only on INTEL_DEBUG(DEBUG_NO_CCS). Patching one does nothing to the other --
which is why replacing INTEL_DEBUG=noccs with 0003 left everything ARC renders
through GL still corrupted while the Vulkan path came good.

Measured on 8086:64a0 with eglQueryDmaBufModifiersEXT, for each of
AR24/XR24/AB24/NV12:

  stock, no noccs   LINEAR, X_TILED, 4_TILED, 4_TILED_LNL_CCS   (1 of 4 CCS)
  stock, noccs      LINEAR, X_TILED, 4_TILED                    (0 of 3)
  patched, no noccs LINEAR, X_TILED, 4_TILED                    (0 of 3)

i.e. the patch reproduces exactly the modifier list noccs produced, for the GL
path as 0003 does for the Vulkan one, while leaving render target compression,
fast clears and sampler decompression alone.

Returning false from modifier_is_supported() covers every entry point, because
they all funnel through it: iris_query_dmabuf_modifiers(),
iris_is_dmabuf_modifier_supported(), select_best_modifier() and
iris_resource_create_with_modifiers().

BMG is de-advertised for the same reason and for symmetry with the other two
patches; this package only ever installs on Lunar Lake, so it is not reachable
in practice.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/iris/iris_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/iris/iris_resource.c
@@ -134,13 +134,36 @@
          return false;
       break;
    case I915_FORMAT_MOD_4_TILED_LNL_CCS:
-      if (devinfo->ver < 20 || devinfo->has_local_mem)
-         return false;
-      break;
    case I915_FORMAT_MOD_4_TILED_BMG_CCS:
-      if (devinfo->ver < 20 || !devinfo->has_local_mem)
-         return false;
-      break;
+      /* brunch: never advertise the Xe2 CCS modifiers.
+       *
+       * iris does not share ANV's modifier filtering: ANV goes through
+       * isl_drm_modifier_get_score() in src/intel/isl/isl_drm.c, iris comes
+       * here. Both have to be patched -- see
+       * mesa-patches/0003-isl-do-not-advertise-xe2-ccs-modifiers.patch and
+       * kernel-patches/7.1/chromeos/0002-lnl_bmg_ccs_deadvertise.patch for the
+       * other two halves.
+       *
+       * The consumer on this system is a ChromeOS R149 image whose minigbm
+       * predates Lunar Lake and has no entry for these modifiers: when a
+       * buffer that gets exported is given a CCS layout, the importer reads it
+       * as plain 4-tiled and the compressed bytes show up as pixels. Every ARC
+       * window rendered through GL (the Play Store, the Play badge splash, the
+       * layers composited over a resized app) came out as vertical stripe
+       * noise with the coarse layout still intact.
+       *
+       * Only the *shared* layout is given up. Internal CCS -- render target
+       * compression, fast clears, sampler decompression -- is untouched, which
+       * is what makes this preferable to INTEL_DEBUG=noccs: that also disables
+       * aux surfaces everywhere (isl.c:3902) and costs bandwidth on everything
+       * drawn, not just on buffers that cross a process boundary.
+       *
+       * Returning false here covers every entry point, because they all funnel
+       * through this function: iris_query_dmabuf_modifiers(),
+       * iris_is_dmabuf_modifier_supported(), select_best_modifier() and
+       * iris_resource_create_with_modifiers().
+       */
+      return false;
    case DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID:
    default:
       return false;
